{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I know month-end close is a bad time for this. I looked into it, and your account locked after several wrong password attempts this morning. They all came from the office network, so nothing looks suspicious. I've asked for your account to be unlocked, and a technician needs to approve that. Once they do, you can sign in again with your current password. Before you try again, please check your phone's mail app and any other device where your password is saved, and update it if it's old. Otherwise the account could lock again. If you can't remember your password, reply and tell us, and we'll arrange a reset. The temporary password would be given to you by phone.",
  "internal_note": "Sender verified as the account owner (Tom Becker, user_id 4, Finance). Account status is 'locked' (not disabled), with failed_login_count 5. Sign-in logs show 5 failed_password attempts on Fri 10/09 between 10:11 and 10:26 ET, all from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York, during work hours. There are no hosting-network or foreign sign-ins, and earlier sign-ins all succeeded with Duo push. This looks like a normal user lockout (likely a mistyped or saved old password), so KB-031 doesn't apply. Queued unlock_account (approval id 1) per KB-001. No password reset requested because the password was last set 2026-07-21 and the user hasn't said they forgot it; issue one only if they ask. Escalate if the account locks again within an hour after saved passwords are updated.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-001"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
